---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Operations Management & People Leadership" current="/operations-leadership/" description="Richard Allen's operations and people-leadership experience across SaaS support, workforce operations, reporting, process improvement, coaching, strategic goal alignment, project coordination, and warehouse management.">
<section class="role-hero ops-hero"><div class="container role-hero-grid">
  <div class="role-hero-copy">
    <div class="eyebrow light">Operations Management & People Leadership</div>
    <h1>Build the operating system around the people doing the work.</h1>
    <p>My operations experience spans people management, workflow coordination, reporting, coaching, strategic goal alignment, process improvement, service delivery, cross-functional work, and earlier warehouse and supply operations.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button button-light" href="/case-studies/">See leadership case studies</a><a class="role-hero-link" href="/resume/">View résumé →</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="ops-console" aria-label="Operations leadership model connecting people, goals, workflow, reporting, and improvement">
    <div class="console-label">OPERATING SYSTEM</div>
    <div class="console-grid">
      <div class="console-cell teal-cell"><span>PEOPLE</span><strong>32</strong><small>support & technical-support reps managed</small></div>
      <div class="console-cell blue-cell"><span>GOALS</span><strong>ALIGN</strong><small>Hoshin Kanri + cascading SMART goals</small></div>
      <div class="console-cell gold-cell"><span>REPORT</span><strong>20+</strong><small>recurring & ad-hoc workforce reports</small></div>
      <div class="console-cell violet-cell"><span>IMPROVE</span><strong>125+</strong><small>SOP program supporting repeatable work</small></div>
    </div>
    <div class="console-footer"><span>coach</span><i>→</i><span>measure</span><i>→</i><span>adjust</span><i>→</i><span>reinforce</span></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="ops-proof-band"><div class="container ops-proof-grid" aria-label="Selected operations scope">
  <div><strong>32</strong><span>representatives managed as Customer Support Manager</span></div>
  <div><strong>400+</strong><span>position records managed across multiple OHA divisions</span></div>
  <div><strong>~20</strong><span>people typically supervised in Aramark warehouse operations</span></div>
  <div><strong>$1M+</strong><span>inventory managed annually in earlier supply operations</span></div>
</div></section>

<section class="section ops-rhythm-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Management rhythm</div><h2>People leadership connected to goals, information, and follow-through.</h2></div><p class="section-note">The pattern is consistent: clarify expectations, coach the work, make performance visible, and improve the system around the team.</p></div>
  <div class="management-rhythm" aria-label="Operations management rhythm">
    <div><span>01</span><strong>Hire & onboard</strong><small>Build capability and set expectations.</small></div><i>→</i>
    <div><span>02</span><strong>Align</strong><small>Connect company priorities to team and individual goals.</small></div><i>→</i>
    <div><span>03</span><strong>Coach</strong><small>Use stand-ups, one-on-ones, quality review, and feedback.</small></div><i>→</i>
    <div><span>04</span><strong>Measure</strong><small>Use reporting and operating data to make work visible.</small></div><i>→</i>
    <div><span>05</span><strong>Improve</strong><small>Adjust process, coverage, training, or policy when evidence shows friction.</small></div>
  </div>
  <div class="strategy-callout"><div><span>STRATEGY DEPLOYMENT</span><strong>From company priorities to individual work</strong></div><p>At HawkSoft, used Hoshin Kanri and cascading SMART goals to create a line of sight from organizational priorities through leadership, departments, teams, and individual employees.</p></div>
</div></section>

<section class="section ops-evidence-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Operations in practice</div><h2>Evidence across people, reporting, process, and delivery.</h2></div><p class="section-note">The management story is broader than supervision alone.</p></div>
  <div class="grid two value-grid ops-card-grid">
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">LEAD</div><h3>People management at scale</h3><p>At HawkSoft, managed 21 people as Team Lead before promotion to Customer Support Manager in 2015, then managed 32 Customer Support and Technical Support representatives, not including four team leads. Responsibilities included hiring and disciplinary authority, performance management, quality review, workload coverage, escalations, stand-ups, and one-on-one coaching.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">DATA</div><h3>Reporting & workforce visibility</h3><p>Turned large support and phone-system exports into management reporting at HawkSoft. At Oregon Health Authority, managed 400+ position records and audited a monthly personnel-error report derived from roughly 3,000 employees, reviewing about 30 fields per employee in my ~400-person area and helping identify and correct hundreds of employment-record errors, including payroll-related issues.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">FLOW</div><h3>Cross-functional service operations</h3><p>Coordinated support coverage, escalations, releases, troubleshooting, migrations, and operational priorities across customer-facing and technical teams. At Marion County, coordinated scheduling, intake, service workflows, reporting, data accuracy, onboarding, and cross-training in a confidential environment.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">125+</div><h3>Process governance & consistency</h3><p>At Oregon Employment Department, led a year-long SOP modernization and governance program across roughly 10 functional groups. The program ultimately encompassed 125+ SOPs, including 25+ legacy procedures inventoried and updated, with standardized templates, review controls, contributor coaching, and centralized storage.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">SUPPLY</div><h3>Warehouse & supply operations</h3><p>Earlier at Aramark Foodservice, typically supervised about 20 people while overseeing purchasing and supply duties, receiving, storage, distribution, shipping, sanitation, and driver or small-fleet activity for more than $1 million in inventory annually.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">STYLE</div><h3>Leadership style</h3><p>Connect organizational priorities to individual work, make performance visible, coach people toward stronger results, and improve the system around them so good work is easier to repeat.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section tight"><div class="container"><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/case-studies/">See case studies</a><a class="button secondary" href="/resume/">View résumé</a><a class="button secondary" href="/contact/">Contact</a></div></div></section>

<style>
  .role-hero{padding:4.8rem 0 4rem;color:#fff;overflow:hidden}.ops-hero{background:radial-gradient(circle at 83% 20%,rgba(15,118,110,.32),transparent 28%),linear-gradient(125deg,#0b2542 0%,#153e75 58%,#0f5b61 100%)}.role-hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.05fr) minmax(360px,.95fr);gap:3rem;align-items:center}.role-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.8rem,6vw,5rem);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:.7rem 0 1.25rem}.role-hero p{font-size:1.15rem;color:#dbe7f1;max-width:720px}.role-hero-link{color:#fff;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;align-self:center}.role-hero-link:hover{color:#c8fff5}.ops-console{padding:1.15rem;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18);border-radius:24px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.07);box-shadow:0 24px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.22);backdrop-filter:blur(8px)}.console-label{font-size:.72rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.16em;color:#c6f1eb;margin:.25rem 0 .8rem}.console-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.7rem}.console-cell{min-height:145px;padding:1rem;border-radius:17px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.13);display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center}.console-cell>span{font-size:.7rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#cbd9e7}.console-cell strong{font-size:2rem;line-height:1.1;margin:.3rem 0;color:#fff}.console-cell small{color:#dce7f0;line-height:1.35}.teal-cell{border-top:4px solid #44c3b5}.blue-cell{border-top:4px solid #68a7f2}.gold-cell{border-top:4px solid #e4b454}.violet-cell{border-top:4px solid #a999ef}.console-footer{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:.9rem .2rem .1rem;color:#d8e6ef;font-size:.78rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em}.console-footer i{font-style:normal;color:#8ea8bd}.ops-proof-band{background:#fff;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.ops-proof-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr)}.ops-proof-grid>div{padding:1.35rem;border-right:1px solid var(--border)}.ops-proof-grid>div:last-child{border-right:0}.ops-proof-grid strong{display:block;font-size:2.1rem;line-height:1;color:var(--accent)}.ops-proof-grid span{display:block;margin-top:.4rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.35}.ops-rhythm-section{background:linear-gradient(180deg,#f5f9fd,#fff)}.management-rhythm{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;align-items:center;gap:.55rem}.management-rhythm>div{min-height:165px;padding:1rem;border-radius:18px;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--border);box-shadow:0 10px 30px rgba(23,32,42,.05)}.management-rhythm>div span{display:grid;place-items:center;width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--blue-soft);color:var(--accent-2);font-weight:900;font-size:.72rem;margin-bottom:.8rem}.management-rhythm>div:nth-of-type(2) span{background:var(--teal-soft);color:var(--teal)}.management-rhythm>div:nth-of-type(3) span{background:var(--gold-soft);color:var(--gold)}.management-rhythm>div:nth-of-type(4) span{background:var(--violet-soft);color:var(--violet)}.management-rhythm strong{display:block}.management-rhythm small{display:block;color:var(--muted);margin-top:.35rem;line-height:1.4}.management-rhythm>i{font-style:normal;color:#9badbe;font-weight:900}.strategy-callout{margin-top:1.2rem;padding:1.3rem 1.4rem;border-radius:18px;background:linear-gradient(110deg,#153e75,#245d91);color:#fff;display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;gap:1.5rem;align-items:center}.strategy-callout span{display:block;font-size:.7rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#bddbf2}.strategy-callout strong{display:block;font-size:1.3rem;line-height:1.2;margin-top:.2rem}.strategy-callout p{margin:0;color:#e5eef5}.ops-evidence-section{background:#fff}.ops-card-grid .card{transition:transform .18s ease,box-shadow .18s ease}.ops-card-grid .card:hover{transform:translateY(-3px);box-shadow:0 15px 35px rgba(23,32,42,.08)}
  @media(max-width:950px){.role-hero-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.ops-console{max-width:720px}.ops-proof-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.management-rhythm{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.management-rhythm>i{display:none}.strategy-callout{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  @media(max-width:600px){.role-hero{padding:3.4rem 0}.console-grid,.ops-proof-grid,.management-rhythm{grid-template-columns:1fr}.role-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.5rem,12vw,3.8rem)}.console-cell{min-height:115px}.ops-proof-grid>div{border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.ops-proof-grid>div:last-child{border-bottom:0}}
  @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ops-card-grid .card{transition:none}.ops-card-grid .card:hover{transform:none}}
</style>
</BaseLayout>
